<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title></title>
</head>
<body><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>T</span><span>ransdisciplinary education focuses on developing an attitude and way of being that enables individuals to contribute to complex societal challenges (Veltman et al., 2021).</span><span>This</span> <span>requires</span> <span>learning</span> <span>outcomes</span> <span>that</span> <span> focus on </span> <span>both</span></span> <span>process</span> <span> and </span> <span>product</span><span><span> (</span><span>Daneshpour</span><span> &amp; </span><span>Kwegyir</span><span>-Afful</span><span>, 2022; </span><span>Ncter</span><span>, 2025).</span></span></font></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span><b>Process</b></span></span></font></p> <p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>The process involves the knowledge, skills, and attitudes developed during transdisciplinary collaboration.</span><span>Within</span> <span>universities</span> <span> of </span> <span>applied</span> <span> sciences and research </span> <span>universities</span><span> — and in </span> <span>the</span> <span>literature</span><span> — </span><span>there</span> <span> are </span> <span>various</span> <span>frameworks</span> <span>outlining</span> <span> these </span> <span>competencies</span><span>.</span></span></font></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>The list below is </span> <span>an</span> <span>example</span> <span> and </span> <span>can</span> <span> help </span> <span>formulate</span> <span>the</span> <span>knowledge</span><span>, skills, and attitudes </span> <span>you</span> <span> want </span> <span>students</span> <span>to</span> <span>develop</span><span> (e.g., Di </span> <span>Giulio</span><span> &amp; </span><span>Defila</span><span>, 2017; </span><span>Oudenampsen</span> <span> et al., 2024; </span><span>Gulikers</span><span> &amp; Oonk, 2019; </span><span>Ncter</span><span>, 2025).</span></span></font></p><ul style="list-style-type:disc; padding-left:20px; margin:0 0 16px 0;"><li style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>Self</span><span>-awareness</span></span> <span><span>Awareness of the role your own discipline plays </span> <span>in a given</span> <span> issue and its limitations, as well as the ability to recognize the added value of other disciplines and non-academic contributors.</span></span></font></li></ul><ul style="list-style-type:disc; padding-left:20px; margin:0 0 16px 0;"><li style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>Purposeful</span> <span> collaboration</span></span> <span><span>The </span> <span>ability</span> <span>to</span> <span>intentionally</span> <span>shape</span> <span>and</span> <span>organize</span> <span>collaboration</span> <span>and</span> <span>dialogue</span> <span>with</span> <span> stakeholders </span> <span>from</span> <span> diverse </span> <span>backgrounds</span> <span>and</span> <span> disciplines in a way </span> <span>that</span> <span>contributes</span> <span>to</span> <span>solving</span> <span>the</span> <span> issue.</span></span></font></li></ul><ul style="list-style-type:disc; padding-left:20px; margin:0 0 16px 0;"><li style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>Iterative</span> <span> opinion </span> <span>formation</span> <span> and </span> <span>mutual</span> <span>learning</span></span> <span><span>The ability to engage openly in dialogue with people from </span> <span>different backgrounds</span> <span> and disciplines, including non-academics, to influence others’ perspectives and allow your own to evolve.</span></span></font></li></ul><ul style="list-style-type:disc; padding-left:20px; margin:0 0 16px 0;"><li style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>Integrating</span> <span> different perspectives</span></span> <span><span>The </span> <span>ability</span> <span>to</span> <span>integrate</span> <span>your</span> <span>own</span> <span> professional </span> <span>perspective</span> <span>and</span> <span>methods</span> <span>with</span> <span>those</span> <span> of </span> <span>others</span><span> (</span><span>scientific</span><span>, practical, </span><span>and</span> <span>experiential</span> <span> sources) in </span> <span>collaboration</span> <span>with</span> <span>people</span> <span>from</span> <span>other</span> <span> disciplines </span> <span>and</span> <span> non-</span><span>academics</span><span>, </span><span>to</span> <span> co-</span><span>create</span> <span>solutions</span> <span>for</span> <span> complex </span> <span>societal</span> <span>challenges</span><span>.</span><span>This</span> <span>process</span> <span> is </span> <span>also</span> <span>referred</span> <span>to</span> <span> as </span></span><span><span>“</span><span>perspectival</span> <span>agility</span><span>”</span></span><span><span> — more on </span> <span>this</span> <span> at </span> <span>the</span> <span>bottom</span> <span> of </span> <span>the</span> <span> page.</span></span></font></li></ul><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><b>Product</b></span></font></p> <p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>Solutions to complex societal challenges are rarely final. They require ongoing refinement and adaptation to changing circumstances.</span><span>Therefore</span><span>, </span><span>when</span> <span>designing</span> <span> a </span> <span>transdisciplinary</span> <span> education project, </span><span>it’s</span> <span> important </span> <span>to</span> <span>formulate</span></span> <span><span>realistic</span> <span>expectations</span></span> <span><span>regarding</span> <span>learning</span> <span>outcomes</span> <span> in </span> <span>relation</span> <span>to</span> <span>the</span> <span>societal</span> <span> issue.</span></span><span><span>Allow</span> <span>for</span> <span>variation</span> <span> in </span> <span>the</span> <span>final</span> <span> product — in </span> <span>terms</span> <span> of form, </span><span>structure</span><span>, or </span> <span>degree</span> <span> of </span> <span>completion</span><span>.</span></span></font></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>&nbsp;A </span> <span>good</span> <span>final</span> <span> product </span> <span>doesn’t</span> <span>need</span> <span>to</span> <span>be</span><span> “</span><span>finished</span><span>,” but </span> <span>it</span> <span> must </span> <span>be</span> <span>meaningful</span> <span>for</span> <span>both</span> <span>the</span> <span>learning</span> <span>process</span> <span> and </span> <span>the</span> <span>involved</span> <span>practice</span> <span> partners.</span></span></font></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>A </span> <span>transdisciplinary</span> <span> project </span> <span>can</span> <span>yield</span> <span> different types of </span> <span>outcomes</span><span>, </span><span>depending</span> <span> on </span> <span>the</span> <span> issue </span> <span>and</span> <span>the</span> <span>collaboration</span><span> (Losse, 2016):</span></span></font></p><ul style="list-style-type:disc; padding-left:20px; margin:0 0 16px 0;"><li style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span><b>Advice</b></span></span></font></li></ul> <p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>Providing</span> <span>knowledge</span><span>, </span><span>insights</span><span>, or </span> <span>lines</span> <span> of </span> <span>thought</span> <span>that</span> <span>contribute</span> <span>to</span> <span>possible</span> <span> solution</span> <span>directions</span><span>.</span></span></font></p><ul style="list-style-type:disc; padding-left:20px; margin:0 0 16px 0;"><li style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><b>Design</b></span></font></li></ul> <p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>Developing</span> <span> a new </span> <span>idea</span><span>, concept, or experiment </span> <span>that</span> <span>contributes</span> <span>to</span> <span>the</span> <span> issue.</span></span></font></p><ul style="list-style-type:disc; padding-left:20px; margin:0 0 16px 0;"><li style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span><b>Intervention</b></span></span></font></li></ul> <p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>A concrete solution </span> <span>tested</span> <span> in </span> <span>practice</span><span>, </span><span>such</span> <span> as a pilot or prototype.</span></span></font></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>Perspectival</span> <span>Flexibility</span><span>: A </span> <span>Key</span> <span> New Area of Research</span></span></font></p> <p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>This</span> <span> is </span> <span>the</span> <span> term </span> <span>researchers</span> <span>use</span> <span>to</span> <span>describe</span> <span>the</span> <span>process</span> <span> in </span> <span>which</span> <span>individuals</span> <span>can</span> <span>recognize</span><span>, </span><span>interpret</span><span>, </span><span>and</span> <span>analyze</span> <span> different </span> <span>perspectives</span><span>, </span><span>reflect</span> <span> on </span> <span>them</span><span>, </span><span>and</span> <span>potentially</span> <span>adjust</span> <span>their</span> <span>own</span> <span> viewpoint.</span></span></font></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>These skills are </span> <span>essential</span> <span> in </span> <span>transdisciplinary</span> <span>collaborations</span><span>, as </span> <span>the</span> <span>central</span> <span> issues are </span> <span>often</span> <span>so</span> <span> complex </span> <span>that</span> <span>many</span> <span> different </span> <span>perspectives</span> <span>and</span> <span>angles</span> <span> are </span> <span>needed</span> <span>to</span> <span>arrive</span> <span> at </span> <span>effective</span> <span>solutions</span><span>.</span></span></font></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>However</span><span>, </span><span>this</span> <span> is a complex </span> <span>cognitive</span> <span>process</span><span>, </span><span>and</span> <span> research shows </span> <span>that</span> <span>adolescents</span> <span> are </span> <span>increasingly</span> <span>less</span> <span>skilled</span> <span> in </span> <span>this</span> <span> area.</span></span></font></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>That’s</span> <span>why</span> <span>researchers</span> <span> at </span> <span>Avans</span> <span> University of </span> <span>Applied</span> <span> Sciences are </span> <span>conducting</span> <span>two</span> <span> studies </span> <span>aimed</span> <span> at </span> <span>understanding</span> <span>the</span> <span>mechanisms</span> <span>behind</span> <span>this</span></span> <span><span>social-cognitive</span> <span>skill</span></span><span>.</span></font></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>Taking</span> <span>and</span> <span>combining</span> <span>perspectives</span> <span>appears</span> <span>to</span> <span>consist</span> <span> of </span> <span>three</span> <span>subprocesses</span><span>:</span></span></font></p><ol style="list-style-type:decimal; padding-left:20px; margin:0 0 16px 0;"><li style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>Perceiving</span> <span>perspectives</span></span></font></li><li style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>Distinguishing</span> <span>between</span> <span>one’s</span> <span>own</span> <span>and</span> <span>others</span><span>’ </span><span>perspectives</span></span></font></li><li style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>Combining</span> <span>perspectives</span></span></font></li></ol> <p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>People </span> <span>often</span> <span>find</span> <span>it</span> <span>difficult</span> <span>to</span> <span> look </span> <span>beyond</span> <span>their</span> <span>own</span> <span> frame of </span> <span>reference</span><span>, </span><span>which</span> <span>makes</span> <span>it</span> <span>challenging</span> <span>to</span> <span>fully</span> <span>utilize</span> <span>other</span> <span>perspectives</span><span>.</span></span></font></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>Especially</span> <span>when</span> <span> information is </span> <span>contradictory</span><span>, </span><span>it</span> <span>becomes</span> <span> hard </span> <span>to</span> <span>identify</span> <span> common </span> <span>ground</span><span> — even </span> <span>though</span> <span>such</span> <span>commonalities</span> <span> are </span> <span>often</span> <span>essential</span> <span>for</span> <span>resolving</span> <span>conflicts</span> <span> or </span> <span>reaching</span> <span> shared </span> <span>insights</span><span>.</span></span></font></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>As a </span> <span>result</span><span>, </span><span>opportunities</span> <span>to</span> <span>develop</span> <span> new </span> <span>ideas</span> <span>and</span> <span>solutions</span> <span>may</span> <span> go </span> <span>unused</span><span>.</span></span></font></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>The </span> <span>two</span> <span> studies, </span><span>conducted</span> <span>by</span> <span>the</span></span> <span><span>Research Group on </span> <span>Transdisciplinary</span> <span>Collaboration</span> <span> in </span> <span>Education</span></span> <span><span>and</span> <span>the</span></span> <span>Research Group on Brain &amp; Learning</span><span><span>, are </span> <span>currently</span> <span>underway</span><span>. Ultimately</span><span>, </span><span>the</span> <span>researchers</span> <span>aim</span> <span>to</span> <span>provide</span></span> <span><span>concrete tools </span> <span>for</span> <span>higher</span> <span>education</span><span>, </span></span><span><span>so</span> <span>that</span> <span>students</span> <span> are </span> <span>better</span> <span>equipped</span> <span>to</span> <span>collaborate</span> <span> on </span> <span>the</span> <span>societal</span> <span>challenges</span> <span> of </span> <span>today</span> <span>and</span> <span>tomorrow</span><span>.</span></span></font></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>Want </span> <span>to</span> <span>stay</span> <span> up </span> <span>to</span> <span> date on </span> <span>the</span> <span>outcomes</span><span>, </span><span>latest</span> <span>insights</span><span>, </span><span>and</span> <span> practical tools </span> <span>related</span> <span>to</span></span> <span><span>perspectival</span> <span>flexibility</span></span><span>?</span></font></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>Sign</span> <span> up </span> <span>for</span> <span>the</span></span> <span><span>newsletter</span></span> <span><span> or follow </span> <span>the</span></span> <span><span>Avans</span> <span>Future-proof</span> <span>Education</span> <span> Center</span></span> <span> on LinkedIn.</span></font></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>Want </span> <span>to</span> <span>learn</span> <span> more </span> <span>now</span><span>?</span></span></font></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span>Contact </span> <span><span>Associate</span> <span>professor </span> <span>Lara van Peppen</span></span> <a href="mailto:m.vanpeppen@avans.nl" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span><span>m.vanpeppen@avans.nl</span></span></a> <span><span> Or </span> <span>visit</span><span>: </span></span><a href="https://www.avans.nl/onderzoek/projecten/detail/onderwijs-met-perspectief" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span><span>Onderwijs met perspectief: adaptieve ondersteuning bij (het aanleren van) perspectivistische lenigheid | Avans Hogeschool</span></span></a></font></p> <p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span>References</span><span>:</span></span></font></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span style="font-size: 12px;">Daneshpour</span><span style="font-size: 12px;">, H., &amp; </span><span style="font-size: 12px;">Kwegyir</span><span style="font-size: 12px;">-Afful, E. (2022). </span><span style="font-size: 12px;">Analysing</span><span style="font-size: 12px;"> </span><span style="font-size: 12px;"> transdisciplinary education: a scoping review. Science &amp; Education, 31(4), 1047-1074.</span></span></font></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><font><span><span style="font-size: 12px;">Gulikers</span><span style="font-size: 12px;">, J., &amp; Oonk, C. (2019). </span><span style="font-size: 12px;">Towards</span><span style="font-size: 12px;"> </span><span style="font-size: 12px;"> a </span><span style="font-size: 12px;"> </span><span style="font-size: 12px;">rubric</span><span style="font-size: 12px;"> </span><span style="font-size: 12px;">for</span><span style="font-size: 12px;"> </span><span style="font-size: 12px;">stimulating</span><span style="font-size: 12px;"> </span><span style="font-size: 12px;">and</span><span style="font-size: 12px;"> </span><span style="font-size: 12px;">evaluating</span><span style="font-size: 12px;"> </span><span style="font-size: 12px;">sustainable</span><span style="font-size: 12px;"> </span><span style="font-size: 12px;">learning</span><span style="font-size: 12px;">. </span><span style="font-size: 12px;">Sustainability</span><span style="font-size: 12px;">, 11(4), 969.</span></span></font></p><p style="line-height: 1.6; margin: 0px 0px 1em;"><span style="font-size: 12px;">Losse, M. (2016) De relevantie van onderzoekend vermogen. Thema Hoger onderwijs, 2016 (1), 57-62.</span></p><p style="line-height: 1.6; margin: 0px 0px 1em;"><span style="font-size: 12px;">Ncter. (2025). Recognising  and Fostering Quality in Transdisciplinary Collaborations for Confronting Societal Challenges.<span style="font-size: 12px;"> </span></span><a href="https://www.transdisciplinairwerken.nl/whitepaper" target="_blank"><span style="font-size: 12px;">https://www.transdisciplinairwerken.nl/whitepaper</span></a><a href="https://www.transdisciplinairwerken.nl/whitepaper" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-size: 1rem;"><span style="font-size: 12px;"></span></a></p><p style="line-height: 1.6; margin: 0px 0px 1em;"><span style="font-size: 12px;">Oudenampsen, J., Das, E., Blijlevens, N., &amp; van de Pol, M. H. (2024). The state of the empirical evidence for interdisciplinary learning outcomes in higher education: A systematic review. The Review of Higher Education, 47(4), 467-518.</span></p><p style="line-height: 1.6; margin: 0px 0px 1em;"><span style="font-size: 12px;">Veltman, M. E., Van Keulen, J., &amp; Voogt, J. M. (2021). Using problems with wicked tendencies as vehicles for learning in higher professional education: Towards coherent curriculum design. The Curriculum Journal, 32(3), 559-583.</span></p></body>
</html>